    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104854" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρι-γενής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>thrice-born,</i> of the
			three stages in the life of moths and the like , <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>GA</u>
				759a3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>of threefold gender,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Trypho
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Pron.</u>
				61.18
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pron.</u>
				105.23
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>of three kinds,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγγεῖα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					14.698
				</span></i>
			; <i>threefold, triple,</i> Anatolius ap. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Theol.Ar.</u>
				35
			</span></i>.</div>
